Yes. Let's restart cleanly from zero. We'll do it step-by-step and verify each stage before moving on.

Your goal:

FastAPI container
      ↓
MySQL container
      ↓
SQLAlchemy
      ↓
auth tables
Step 1 — Make sure old Compose resources are gone

From your project folder:

cd /Users/nidhikumari/Desktop/FASTAPICRUD

Run:

docker compose down -v --remove-orphans

Then check:

docker ps -a
docker images

You don't need to manually delete anything else.

Step 2 — Fix docker-compose.yml

Use this structure:

services:
  db:
    image: mysql:8.0
    container_name: mysql_container
    environment:
      MYSQL_ALLOW_EMPTY_PASSWORD: "yes"
      MYSQL_DATABASE: fastapi_db
    volumes:
      - mysql_data:/var/lib/mysql
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "mysqladmin", "ping", "-h", "localhost"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5

  fastapi:
    build: .
    container_name: fastapi_app
    depends_on:
      db:
        condition: service_healthy
    ports:
      - "8000:8000"
    environment:
      MYSQL_HOST: db
      MYSQL_PORT: 3306
      MYSQL_DATABASE: fastapi_db
      MYSQL_USER: root
      MYSQL_PASSWORD: ""

volumes:
  mysql_data:

Important: Notice there is no ports: 3306:3306 under MySQL. Your Mac's local MySQL is already using 3306.

Step 3 — Check .dockerignore

It should contain only:

myvenv/
__pycache__/
.git/
.env
.DS_Store

Definitely no Dockerfile commands inside .dockerignore.

Step 4 — Check Dockerfile

Use:

FROM python:3.11-slim

WORKDIR /app

COPY requirements.txt .

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

COPY . .

EXPOSE 8000

CMD ["uvicorn", "auth.main:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000"]
Step 5 — Validate Compose

Run:

docker compose config

If there is no error, run:

docker compose config --services

Expected:

db
fastapi
Step 6 — Build and start everything
docker compose up --build -d

Wait about 10–15 seconds.

Then:

docker compose ps

Expected:

mysql_container   ...   Up (healthy)
fastapi_app       ...   Up
STOP HERE

Don't create the table yet.

Send me the output of:

docker compose ps


